            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.163
          ],
          "content": "This way of associating each cow with a stick, such that no two cows are associated or mapped to the same stick is called a one-to-one mapping. This mapping can then be used to come up with a way to represent numbers, as shown in the table."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.27,
            0.166,
            0.728,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": "| Number | Its representation (using sticks) |\n| --- | --- |\n| 12345... | ... |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_table_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.414,
            0.847,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": "? How will you use such sticks to answer the other two questions (Q2 and Q3)?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.458,
            0.849,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": "**Method 2:** Instead of objects, we could use a standard sequence of sounds or names. For example, we could use the sounds of the letters of any language. While counting, we could make a one-to-one mapping between the objects and the letters: that is, associate each object to be counted with a letter, following the letter-order. This mapping can then be used to come up with a way of verbally representing numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.569,
            0.847,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": "For example, we get the following number representation if we use English letters ‘a’ to ‘z’."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.282,
            0.618,
            0.716,
            0.887
          ],
          "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">Number</td><td rowspan=\"2\">Its representation (using sounds or names)</td></tr><tr></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>a</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>b</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>c</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>d</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>e</td></tr><tr><td>.</td><td>.</td></tr><tr><td>.</td><td>.</td></tr><tr><td>.</td><td>.</td></tr><tr><td>26</td><td>z</td></tr></tbody></table>",
